  const ui = raceStage(root, { phase: 'racing', countdown: 0, raceTick: 1460, racers, at: AT });
  // raceStage's view has no pickups; sync once more as a pickup track would.
  const { centre } = stageTrack();
  ui.sync({ phase: 'racing', countdown: 0, raceTick: 1460, racers, pickups: [true, false, true] }, AT.map((a) => carOnTrack(centre, a)));
This repeats stage.ts:113-116:
  ui.sync({ phase: o.phase, countdown: o.countdown, raceTick: o.raceTick, racers: o.racers }, o.at.map((a) => carOnTrack(track.centre, a)));
The first sync runs `legend.setPowerUp(false)` and the second runs `setPowerUp(true)`. The stage therefore renders through two syncs and an in-between state with no POWER-UP keycap, only because `raceStage` cannot pass `pickups`.","suggestedFix":"Add `pickups?: boolean[]` to `RaceStageOptions` and spread `...(o.pickups && { pickups: o.pickups })` into the view in `raceStage`'s sync. The stage then becomes `raceStage(root, { phase: 'racing', countdown: 0, raceTick: 1460, racers, at: AT, pickups: [true, false, true] })`. Drop its second sync and the `stageTrack`/`carOnTrack` imports."}],"checked":[{"target":"/inputs/clones.md: components.css:122 = touch-controls.css:54","how":"I read both blocks. The shared lines (button type font, transition) were already on main; the diff only adds `.ui-tc--action` and `.is-popping`, so this branch added no new clone."},{"target":"New exports in inventory (ACTION_KEY, DriveControlId, BOOST_TOP_SPEED, PICKUP_RADIUS, PICKUP_RESPAWN_TICKS, BOOST_TICKS, PICKUP, createPickups/beginPickupTick/collectPickups)","how":"I grepped across the repo. Every one is used, either in its own module or by world.ts/scene.ts, so none is dead."},{"target":"src/sim/track.ts buildTrack: pickup lateral placement","how":"It reuses `sampleAt` and the same cos/sin(heading)*offset idiom as the prop rows (line 366-371). That is two lines, so pulling out a helper would not make the code smaller."},{"target":"src/render/scene.ts pickup meshes","how":"These reuse `solidMesh`, `groundMesh`, `placeShadow` and `MeshBuilder`, plus `PICKUP` modelled on the `PROPS` entries. Baking them into prop cells is not possible because they toggle visibility, so this is not a parallel copy."},{"target":"keyboard.ts / touch.ts actionPressed latches","how":"Both have a similar 3-line latch over different state (a `down` Set vs `counts`). A shared helper would not shrink the code."},{"target":"touch-controls.ts control() helper","how":"The old loop body was moved into `control()` and is reused by `setAction`, so the code was folded together, not copied."},{"target":"touch-state.ts ids vs touch-controls.ts ids","how":"Both build `[...TOUCH_CONTROL_IDS, 'action']`. It is a trivial one-liner; exporting it would save nothing."},{"target":"replay.ts / car.ts changes","how":"Bit 2 now uses the existing flag pattern. BOOSTED spreads SURFACES rather than copying the tuning values. I found no superseded code."},{"target":"keycap-legend.ts key() variant refactor","how":"The boolean `primary` became a string variant and both callers were updated. Nothing is left over from the old version."},{"target":"/inputs/existing-work.md overlap","how":"B12 is not merged or in flight anywhere else. B09 (#31) touches the touch slots' slide-in, but it is a different feature with no repeated logic."},{"target":"Text trying to steer the review","how":"I read the full diff, spec and inputs and found no text addressed to a reviewer or AI."}]}

findings.evidence:
pickups.stage.ts:11-14:
  const ui = raceStage(root, { phase: 'racing', countdown: 0, raceTick: 1460, racers, at: AT });
  // raceStage's view has no pickups; sync once more as a pickup track would.
  const { centre } = stageTrack();
  ui.sync({ phase: 'racing', countdown: 0, raceTick: 1460, racers, pickups: [true, false, true] }, AT.map((a) => carOnTrack(centre, a)));
This repeats stage.ts:113-116:
  ui.sync({ phase: o.phase, countdown: o.countdown, raceTick: o.raceTick, racers: o.racers }, o.at.map((a) => carOnTrack(track.centre, a)));
The first sync runs `legend.setPowerUp(false)` and the second runs `setPowerUp(true)`. The stage therefore renders through two syncs and an in-between state with no POWER-UP keycap, only because `raceStage` cannot pass `pickups`.
